  "title": "Svetitskhoveli Cathedral, Mtskheta",
  "summary": "Svetitskhoveli Cathedral in Mtskheta, Georgia, was built between 1010 and 1029 under Catholicos Melchizedek to a design by the architect Arsukidze. It replaced earlier churches on the site, the first a wooden one from the 4th century, and is the largest surviving church in Georgia.",
